From d43ad80f47246b4b30d5e7f4020a205eb87912e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: erranter <erranter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:41:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix(desktop): keep the remote runtime sync running
 without a console window

Two changes. The SSH runner now asks for the base release version, because fork builds append a release suffix to appVersion while the runtime archives stay under the v0.1.5 tag; the old value made the bootstrap download a tag that does not exist. And the one-off Windows task that pre-seeds those archives is rewritten once to a wscript launcher at a 15 minute cadence, so it keeps syncing without a console window flashing every minute.
